### Page 6 of 6

```text
Board of County Commissioners
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
October 1, 2024
Justin Arnold, Planning, said Steil Surveying Services, LLC, on behalf of G & G
Enterprises of Wyoming, LLC, submitted an administrative plat application for
Cheyenne Pass, 2nd Filing, situated in a portion of Sect 11, T14N, R70W, 6th PM,
Laramie County, WY. He said the subject property lies at 415 Lynx Ln, and the
application combines both parcels, creating a 6.92-acre lot for residential use and
correcting a problem with setbacks on a residence currently being built.
Arnold said based on evidence provided, staff recommends approval with the
adoption of findings of fact a and b with no conditions.
Chairman Lovett opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Hearing no PUBLIC
COMMENT, Chairman Lovett closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Commissioner Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Holmes, that this agenda item be approved. The motion
carried by the following vote:
Lovett, Malm, Heath, Holmes, Thompson
Aye:
The meeting adjourned at 3:48 pm.
CERTIFICATION
I, Debra K. Lee, Clerk of Laramie County, do hereby certify the above to be a true
and correct copy of the Minutes of the Proceedings for Tuesday, Oct 1, 2024.
Approved by : Debra K. Lee, County Clerk
Reviewed by : Gunnar Malm, Acting Chairman,
Board of County Commissioners
Reasonable Accommodations
This information is available in alternate forms.  If reasonable accommodations are
required, contact Laramie County Human Resources at (307) 633-4355 or
humanresources@laramiecountywy.gov at least two business days prior to the
meeting. Per WS §18-3-516(f), access to county information can be obtained at
laramiecountywy.gov.
